  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/gorc1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. 2026-11-01 review (dev 100b6fbb6e): register(Map[int]) and S{Handler: Map[int]} still emit no reference edge (Plain controls do). Part 2 reproduces but is broader: Plain(x).Bar() (non-generic conversion) is also untyped (external 0.4), and a method on a generic receiver func (b Box[T]) Foo() is emitted as bare Foo (not Box.Foo) because _extract_receiver_type_from_node handles only type_identifier/pointer_type, so even typed x.Foo() is ambiguous. Suggest split: value arms / conversion-call typing / generic-receiver method naming. MECHANISM: value-reference arms read no index_expression; conversion-call results carry no type; generic receiver type nodes unread. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-nulig."  # 8298
